# COUNTERMOVEMENT JUMP

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Countermovement Jump (CMJ) is an explosive lower-body exercise performed using a rapid downward movement immediately followed by maximal vertical propulsion.

Within CAS, it serves both as a power-development exercise and as a key assessment of neuromuscular readiness.

---

# Philosophy

Power is not only measured by how much force an athlete can produce.

It is measured by how quickly that force can be produced.

The Countermovement Jump develops explosive triple extension while simultaneously providing valuable information about fatigue and readiness.

CAS frequently uses the CMJ both as a training exercise and as a monitoring tool.

